-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ו/8 (16.7.2026): קצובת ביגוד
-- The clothing allowance for school year תשפ"ו, the additional allowances
-- for physical-education teachers, for technological education and for
-- physiotherapists in Ofek Hadash or Oz LaTmura.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time in the regulative rules is counted in school months of תשפ"ו
-- (common.l4: September 2025 = 1, July 2026 = 11, August 2026 = 12).

§ `תשפ"ו/8 קצובת ביגוד`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date (16.7.2026), reference number, addressee and the subject line with its four topics; no rule.

DECLARE `clothing action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the clothing allowance` HAS `clothing amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the physical-education allowance` HAS `physical-education amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the technological-education allowance` HAS `technological amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the physiotherapists' allowance` HAS `physiotherapy amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `employ beyond the limits` HAS `position employed` IS A NUMBER

§§ `1 קצובת ביגוד לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ו`

-- akn:art_1/p1 The heading "תחולה"; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p4 The heading "כללי"; no rule.

-- Section 1 applies to every employee graded on the teaching-staff scale
-- employed by an owning body the Ministry supervises; the Treasury's
-- instructions on the clothing allowance are followed as below.
@ref akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1/p3
GIVEN `graded as teaching staff` IS A BOOLEAN, `employed by a supervised owning body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1 applies to` `graded as teaching staff` `employed by a supervised owning body` IF
    `graded as teaching staff` AND `employed by a supervised owning body`

-- 1.ב–1.ג: entitled as public-facing civil servants are, for school year
-- תשפ"ו (09/25–08/26), at level 4: 2,527.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_1__para_c
`the clothing allowance at level 4` MEANS 2527

-- 1.ד: in proportion to the position, one full position at most; 1.ה: with
-- more than one employer, each pays on the position held with it, even
-- where the total passes 100%.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d akn:art_1__para_e
GIVEN `position fraction with this employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `clothing allowance` `position fraction with this employer` IS
    `the clothing allowance at level 4` TIMES min `position fraction with this employer` 1

@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN `position fraction with this employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `clothing allowance paid in full with July's salary` `position fraction with this employer` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the clothing allowance` a
          PROVIDED a AT LEAST `clothing allowance` `position fraction with this employer`
    WITHIN `month number` July
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ו/8 §1.א: the clothing allowance is paid in full with July 2026's salary"

DECLARE `employment terms` IS ONE OF
    `teaching employee outside the reform`
    `principal outside the reform`
    `teacher in full implementation of Oz LaTmura`
    `teacher in Ofek Hadash`

-- 1.ו: 140% across all employers for a teaching employee, 150% for a
-- principal outside the reform; 131.5% in full Oz LaTmura and 117% in Ofek
-- Hadash, subject to the exceptional-employment procedure for תשפ"ו. A
-- reform teacher is also a teaching employee, so the stricter limit binds.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f akn:art_1__para_f/p2
GIVEN t IS AN `employment terms`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position limit across all employers` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `teaching employee outside the reform` THEN 1.4
    WHEN `principal outside the reform` THEN 1.5
    WHEN `teacher in full implementation of Oz LaTmura` THEN 1.315
    WHEN `teacher in Ofek Hadash` THEN 1.17

-- akn:art_1__para_f/p4 The address of the exceptional-employment procedure; the procedure itself is not in the corpus.

-- The closing paragraph of 1: nothing above changes the conditions for
-- approval of these positions or permits employment beyond them.
@ref akn:art_1/p5 akn:art_1__para_f/p3
GIVEN t IS AN `employment terms`, `approved under the exceptional-employment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `no employment beyond the limits` t `approved under the exceptional-employment procedure` IS
    IF `approved under the exceptional-employment procedure`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         SHANT `employ beyond the limits` p
               PROVIDED p GREATER THAN `the position limit across all employers` t
         WITHIN 12
         LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ו/8 §1: no permit to employ beyond the position limits"

§§ `2 קצובת ביגוד נוספת למורה לחינוך גופני`

@desc A row of a part-time table: an employment rate and the amount it pays as at the date the table prints.
DECLARE `rate band` HAS
    `band above`           IS A NUMBER   @desc the band starts above this rate (or at it, where `band from inclusive`)
    `band from inclusive`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `band up to`           IS A NUMBER   @desc the band ends at this rate (or below it, where not `band to inclusive`); 999 stands for no upper bound
    `band to inclusive`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `band amount`          IS A NUMBER

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER, b IS A `rate band`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rate falls in` r b IF
        (    (b's `band from inclusive` AND r AT LEAST b's `band above`)
          OR ((NOT b's `band from inclusive`) AND r GREATER THAN b's `band above`))
    AND (    (b's `band to inclusive` AND r AT MOST b's `band up to`)
          OR ((NOT b's `band to inclusive`) AND r LESS THAN b's `band up to`))

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER, table IS A LIST OF `rate band`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the amounts the table gives for` r table IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `band amount`) (filter (GIVEN b YIELD `the rate falls in` r b) table)

GIVEN table IS A LIST OF `rate band`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every rate has exactly one row in` table IF
    all (GIVEN r YIELD count (`the amounts the table gives for` r table) EQUALS 1)
        (LIST 0, 0.1, 0.29, 0.2999, 0.3, 0.31, 0.45, 0.5, 0.5001, 0.51, 0.75, 1)

-- "עד 30% לא כולל" · "מ-30% ועד 50% כולל" · "מעל 50%", as at 1.9.2026
-- (F-2025-26_tashpo_08-b: a date after the school year the allowance is for),
-- updating the amounts of circular תשע"ב/8 (not restated here).
@ref akn:art_2/p2 akn:art_2/t1
`the physical-education table` MEANS
    LIST `rate band` 0   TRUE  0.3 FALSE 0,
         `rate band` 0.3 TRUE  0.5 TRUE  806.07,
         `rate band` 0.5 FALSE 999 TRUE  1607.93

#ASSERT `every rate has exactly one row in` `the physical-education table`

-- F-2025-26_tashpo_08-b: both part-time tables print their amounts as
-- correct for 1/9/2026, the first day of the school year AFTER the one the
-- allowances are for (09/25–08/26), and after July 2026, when §1 and §4 are
-- paid. Months counted as year × 12 + month. The reading adopted: the
-- printed amounts are paid for תשפ"ו as they stand.
`the tables' date` MEANS 2026 TIMES 12 PLUS 9
`the last month of school year תשפ"ו` MEANS 2026 TIMES 12 PLUS 8
`the tables' amounts are dated after the school year they are paid for` MEANS
    `the tables' date` GREATER THAN `the last month of school year תשפ"ו`
#ASSERT `the tables' amounts are dated after the school year they are paid for`

GIVEN `employment rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `physical-education allowance` `employment rate` IS
    sum (`the amounts the table gives for` `employment rate` `the physical-education table`)

-- 2, first paragraph: in addition to the general clothing allowance, and
-- it covers sun-protection products. The circular sets no month for it,
-- so the duty carries no deadline.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN `employment rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `physical-education allowance paid` `employment rate` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the physical-education allowance` a
          PROVIDED a AT LEAST `physical-education allowance` `employment rate`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ו/8 §2: the physical-education teacher's additional clothing allowance for תשפ\"ו"

§§ `3 קצובת ביגוד בחינוך הטכנולוגי`

-- 3.1א's table: a pair of shoes and two robes a year.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_a akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_a/t1
`the professions with shoes and two robes` MEANS
    LIST "מערכות תעופה", "מכטרוניקה", "טרמודינמיקה טכנית ימית", "מערכות סיב\"מ ותיב\"מ",
         "תחזוקת מערכות מכניות", "מערכות מכונאות רכב", "מערכות ממוחשבות ברכב",
         "מערכות הספק, פיקוד ובקרה", "מערכות בקרת אקלים", "אומנות הבישול והאפיה המלונאית",
         "ימאות – ספינות", "מערכות טלוויזיה וקולנוע", "מערכות צילום"

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_a/p2
`the value of a pair of shoes and two robes` MEANS 663.14

-- 3.1ב's table: two robes a year.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_b akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_b/t1
`the professions with two robes` MEANS
    LIST "מערכות אלקטרוניות", "מערכות מחשוב ובקרה", "מערכות מחשבים", "תכנון ותכנות מערכות",
         "מערכות ביוטכנולוגיה", "ניהול תיירותי", "ניהול מלונאי",
         "חינוך לגיל הרך", "עיצוב", "אופנה ותלבושות", "עיצוב שיער, וטיפוח החן", "סיעוד", "אומנות שימושית"

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_b/p2
`the value of two robes` MEANS 411.97

-- The two lists are disjoint, thirteen professions each, so no profession
-- is given two allowances.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD NOT elem p `the professions with two robes`) `the professions with shoes and two robes`
#ASSERT count `the professions with shoes and two robes` EQUALS 13 AND count `the professions with two robes` EQUALS 13

-- 3.3: in proportion to the position in technological education, one
-- full position at most. 3.2: in addition to the general allowance.
@ref akn:art_3/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-2 akn:art_3__para_3-3
GIVEN `profession` IS A STRING, `position fraction in technological education` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `technological-education allowance` `profession` `position fraction in technological education` IS
    (IF elem `profession` `the professions with shoes and two robes`
     THEN `the value of a pair of shoes and two robes`
     ELSE IF elem `profession` `the professions with two robes`
          THEN `the value of two robes`
          ELSE 0)
    TIMES min `position fraction in technological education` 1

-- As for §2, the circular sets no month for it.
GIVEN `profession` IS A STRING, `position fraction in technological education` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `technological-education allowance paid` `profession` `position fraction in technological education` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the technological-education allowance` a
          PROVIDED a AT LEAST `technological-education allowance` `profession` `position fraction in technological education`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ו/8 §3: the technological-education clothing allowance for תשפ\"ו"

§§ `4 קצובת ביגוד לפיזיותרפיסטים`

@ref akn:art_4/p1
GIVEN `teaching employee in the health professions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holds a physiotherapy certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treats by physiotherapy in the teaching role` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a physiotherapist` `teaching employee in the health professions` `holds a physiotherapy certificate` `treats by physiotherapy in the teaching role` IF
        `teaching employee in the health professions`
    AND `holds a physiotherapy certificate`
    AND `treats by physiotherapy in the teaching role`

-- 4, second paragraph: a full-time physiotherapist in Ofek Hadash or Oz
-- LaTmura: 800 "only", once a year with July's salary, in addition to the
-- clothing allowance (citing תשפ"ג/4 §14 and תשפ"ה/5 §15, not restated here).
@ref akn:art_4/p2
`the full-time physiotherapists' allowance` MEANS 800

-- 4, third paragraph and its table: part-time, by the rules of the
-- physical-education allowance, as at 1.9.2026 (F-2025-26_tashpo_08-b).
@ref akn:art_4/p3 akn:art_4/t1
`the physiotherapists' part-time table` MEANS
    LIST `rate band` 0   TRUE  0.3 FALSE 0,
         `rate band` 0.3 TRUE  0.5 TRUE  432.06,
         `rate band` 0.5 FALSE 999 TRUE  864.12

#ASSERT `every rate has exactly one row in` `the physiotherapists' part-time table`

-- F-2025-26_tashpo_08-a: the table's top row ("מעל 50%") pays 864.12,
-- more than the full-time 800, and a full position is itself "above 50%".
`the part-time table pays more than the full-time allowance above 50%` MEANS
    `the amounts the table gives for` 0.6 `the physiotherapists' part-time table`
        EQUALS LIST 864.12
    AND 864.12 GREATER THAN `the full-time physiotherapists' allowance`
    AND `the amounts the table gives for` 1 `the physiotherapists' part-time table`
        EQUALS LIST 864.12
#ASSERT `the part-time table pays more than the full-time allowance above 50%`

-- The reading adopted (F-2025-26_tashpo_08-a): a full position is paid by
-- the second paragraph (800), and the table governs part-time positions.
@export The additional clothing allowance for a physiotherapist in Ofek Hadash or Oz LaTmura for school year תשפ"ו under circular תשפ"ו/8
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc the physiotherapist's position (1 = a full position)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `physiotherapists' allowance` `position fraction` IS
    IF `position fraction` AT LEAST 1
    THEN `the full-time physiotherapists' allowance`
    ELSE sum (`the amounts the table gives for` `position fraction` `the physiotherapists' part-time table`)

GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `physiotherapists' allowance paid with July's salary` `position fraction` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the physiotherapists' allowance` a
          PROVIDED a AT LEAST `physiotherapists' allowance` `position fraction`
    WITHIN `month number` July
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ו/8 §4: the physiotherapists' clothing allowance is paid with July's salary"

-- akn:conclusions The contact line, signatures and copies; no rule.

-- Examples (positions and professions are placeholders; amounts are the circular's).
#ASSERT `clothing allowance` 0.5 EQUALS 1263.5
#ASSERT `clothing allowance` 1.3 EQUALS 2527
#ASSERT `physical-education allowance` 0.29 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `physical-education allowance` 0.3 EQUALS 806.07
#ASSERT `physical-education allowance` 0.5 EQUALS 806.07
#ASSERT `physical-education allowance` 0.51 EQUALS 1607.93
#ASSERT `technological-education allowance` "מכטרוניקה" 1 EQUALS 663.14
#ASSERT `technological-education allowance` "סיעוד" 0.5 EQUALS 205.985
#ASSERT `physiotherapists' allowance` 1 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `physiotherapists' allowance` 0.4 EQUALS 432.06

#TRACE `clothing allowance paid in full with July's salary` 1 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the clothing allowance` 2527 AT 11
#TRACE `physiotherapists' allowance paid with July's salary` 1 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the physiotherapists' allowance` 800 AT 11
#TRACE `no employment beyond the limits` `teacher in Ofek Hadash` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `employ beyond the limits` 1.2 AT 2
